  36:     Move colored sprites from the left strip into a framed area at marker-defined targets.
  37: 
  38:     Input structure:
  39:     - bg background; rectangular frame on right with colored markers on its edges; sprites in a narrow left strip separated by a constant-color divider column.
  40: 
  41:     Rule:
  42:     - For each color, target rows/cols are where both opposite frame edges share that color. Targets are the Cartesian product.
  43:     - Erase each sprite from the left and stamp it centered at every target. Higher sprites cover lower ones.
  44: 
  45:     Key insight: One sprite replicates to a grid of row × column marker intersections.
  46:     """
  47:     g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)
  48:     H, W = g.shape
  49:     bg = int(get_bg(g))
  50: 
  51:     # --- frame interior: largest bg component not touching boundary ---
  52:     inner_bbox = largest_enclosed_component_bbox(g == int(bg), connectivity=4)
  53:     assert not (inner_bbox is None)
  54:     ir0, ic0, ir1, ic1 = map(int, inner_bbox)
  55:     fr0, fc0, fr1, fc1 = int(ir0 - 1), int(ic0 - 1), int(ir1 + 1), int(ic1 + 1)
  56: 
  57:     # --- divider columns (fixed) on the left side ---
  58:     divider_mask = np.zeros((H, W), dtype=bool)
  59:     for c in range(0, max(0, int(fc0))):
  60:         colv = g[:, int(c)]
  61:         non = colv[colv != int(bg)]
  62:         if int(len(non)) >= int(H - 1) and len(set(map(int, non))) == 1:
  63:             divider_mask[:, int(c)] = True
  64: 
  65:     left_cols = (np.arange(W)[None, :] < int(fc0))
  66: 
  67:     # --- sprites: per-color 8-connected components in left area (excluding divider) ---
  68:     sprites = []
  69:     for col in sorted(set(map(int, g.flatten())) - {int(bg)}):
  70:         mask = (g == int(col)) & left_cols & (~divider_mask)
  71:         if not bool(mask.any()):
  72:             continue
  73:         slab, sn = label_mask(mask, connectivity=8)
